      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits beside the Painted Desert, a colorful basin that early explorers called “El Desierto Pintada” after crossing the Little Colorado.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holbrook%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1892 the original depot was replaced by the Santa Fe Depot, a historic station that still stands in downtown Holbrook.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holbrook%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Holbrook hosts the National Historic Landmark Painted Desert Inn, an adobe building that once served travelers on Route 66.",
